    "answer": {
      "short": "Line (3): the square-root product rule requires non-negative factors and cannot be applied to $-1$ and $-1$.",
      "worked": "The first invalid step is from line (2) to line (3). Although $(-1)(-1)=1$, the real square-root law $\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}$ requires $a,b\\geq0$. Here $a=b=-1$, and $\\sqrt{-1}$ is not a real number.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
